WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.292
A scheduled run should
raise only what's new,

2
00:00:03.292 --> 00:00:06.625
so Chapter 06 adds a
comparison by finding I D.

3
00:00:06.625 --> 00:00:07.800
New means raise it.

4
00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:12.462
Persisting means it's already raised,
and the de-duplication adds a counter.

5
00:00:12.462 --> 00:00:14.700
Resolved means it's no longer measured.

6
00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:17.420
That's a lead for the
re-read, not a closure:

7
00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:20.800
its record still closes
only on the re-read client.

8
00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:24.572
And the comparison refuses runs
that computed different classes,

9
00:00:24.572 --> 00:00:26.492
one with the audit and one without,

10
00:00:26.492 --> 00:00:30.950
because every finding of the class the
second run skipped would look resolved.

11
00:00:30.950 --> 00:00:33.762
The lab's day-two fixture
tells a small story.

12
00:00:33.762 --> 00:00:37.280
HR corrects Erin's department
from HR to Finance,

13
00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:41.413
the value someone had already
typed into Entra ID by hand.

14
00:00:41.413 --> 00:00:43.389
Graph now agrees with HR.

15
00:00:43.389 --> 00:00:46.700
SailPoint, not yet re-aggregated, doesn't.
